 1 
 ). MOFs are a type of organic–inorganic hybrid material, also known as coordination polymers. It differs from both inorganic porous materials and organic complexes in general. It has both the rigidity of inorganic materials and the flexibility of organic materials, which shows great development potential and remarkable development prospects in modern materials research. [ 

